# Lumerical MCP Server

MCP (Model Context Protocol) server for controlling Lumerical FDTD simulations from LLMs.

## Installation

```bash
cd lumerical-mcp
pip install -e .
```

## Configuration

### Required Environment Variable

```bash
# Windows (PowerShell)
$env:LUMERICAL_ROOT = "D:\Program Files\ANSYS Inc\v251\Lumerical"

# Windows (cmd)
set LUMERICAL_ROOT=D:\Program Files\ANSYS Inc\v251\Lumerical

# Linux/macOS
export LUMERICAL_ROOT=/opt/lumerical/v251
```

### Optional Environment Variables

| Variable | Default | Description |
|----------|---------|-------------|
| `MCP_HOST` | `127.0.0.1` | Server bind address |
| `MCP_PORT` | `8000` | Server port |
| `MCP_TRANSPORT` | `streamable-http` | Transport protocol (`streamable-http` or `stdio`) |
| `MCP_WORK_DIR` | Current directory | Working directory for relative paths |
| `MCP_LOG_LEVEL` | `INFO` | Log level (`DEBUG`, `INFO`, `WARNING`, `ERROR`) |

### Config File (Optional)

Create `~/.config/lumerical-mcp/config.json`:

```json
{
  "MCP_HOST": "127.0.0.1",
  "MCP_PORT": 8000,
  "MCP_TRANSPORT": "streamable-http",
  "MCP_WORK_DIR": "C:/Users/name/projects/lumerical",
  "MCP_LOG_LEVEL": "INFO"
}
```

Environment variables take precedence over config file.

## Running the Server

```bash
lumerical-mcp
```

Or with custom settings:

```bash
MCP_PORT=9000 MCP_TRANSPORT=stdio lumerical-mcp
```

## Available Tools

| Tool | Description |
|------|-------------|
| `hello` | Connectivity check |
| `start_fdtd` / `end_fdtd` | Start/stop FDTD API session |
| `open_projects` / `fdtd_load_project_tool` | Load `.fsp` project |
| `save_project` / `fdtd_save_project_tool` | Save project |
| `set_parameter` | Set object property |
| `run_simulation` / `fdtd_run_simulation_tool` | Run simulation |
| `get_transmission` | Get transmission spectrum from monitor |
| `fdtd_eval_script_tool` | Execute Lumerical script |
| `fdtd_eval_script_get_tool` | Execute script and return variable |
| `fdtd_run_script_file_tool` | Run `.lsf`/`.lsfx` script file |
| `fdtd_get_variable_tool` / `fdtd_put_variable_tool` | Read/write script variables |
| `fdtd_launch_gui_tool` | Launch Lumerical GUI |
| `fdtd_command_docs_tool` | Search command documentation |

## Client Usage

```bash
# Using the test client
python client_test.py

# Or with custom server address
MCP_HOST=192.168.1.100 MCP_PORT=9000 python client_test.py
```

## LLM Client Configuration

### Claude Desktop (`claude_desktop_config.json`)

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lumerical": {
      "command": "lumerical-mcp",
      "env": {
        "LUMERICAL_ROOT": "D:\\Program Files\\ANSYS Inc\\v251\\Lumerical"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

### VS Code / Continue / Other MCP Clients

```json
{
  "mcpServers": {
    "lumerical": {
      "command": "lumerical-mcp",
      "args": [],
      "env": {
        "LUMERICAL_ROOT": "/opt/lumerical/v251"
      }
    }
  }
}
```

